      {
        "id": "p16-q7a",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$kx^2-(2k-1)x+k=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p16-q7a-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$k=\\frac14$ or $k=0$.",
              "worked": "For $k\\ne0$, the equation is quadratic.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=[-(2k-1)]^2-4(k)(k)\\\\\\Delta&=4k^2-4k+1-4k^2\\\\\\Delta&=1-4k\\\\0&=1-4k\\end{align*}$$\nThus $k=\\tfrac14$.\nWhen $k=0$, the equation becomes $x=0$, which also has one real root.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 23,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q7a-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$k<\\frac14$, with $k\\ne0$.",
              "worked": "Two real roots require a quadratic with $\\Delta>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}1-4k&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $k<\\tfrac14$.\nExclude $k=0$, which gives a linear equation.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 13,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q7a-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$k>\\frac14$.",
              "worked": "A quadratic has no real roots when $\\Delta<0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}1-4k&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThus $k>\\tfrac14$.\nAll values in this range keep the equation quadratic.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 11,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q7b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$4(k+1)x^2+4kx+(k-2)=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p16-q7b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$k=-2$ or $k=-1$.",
              "worked": "For $k\\ne-1$, the equation is quadratic.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(4k)^2-4[4(k+1)](k-2)\\\\\\Delta&=16[k^2-(k+1)(k-2)]\\\\\\Delta&=16(k+2)\\\\0&=16(k+2)\\\\k&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $k=-1$, the equation becomes $-4x-3=0$, with the single real root $x=-\\frac34$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 26,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q7b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$k>-2$, with $k\\ne-1$.",
              "worked": "Two real roots require a quadratic with $\\Delta>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}16(k+2)&>0\\\\k&>-2\\end{align*}$$\nExclude $k=-1$, which gives a linear equation.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 13,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          },
          {
            "id": "p16-q7b-iii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$k<-2$.",
              "worked": "A quadratic has no real roots when $\\Delta<0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}16(k+2)&<0\\\\k&<-2\\end{align*}$$\nAll values in this range keep the equation quadratic.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 11,
            "responseSpace": "scaffold"
          }
